//! Format: MPEG-1, MPEG-2, and MPEG-2.5 Layer III packet decoder component.
//! Supported: Nothing yet decodes. This file is the format's normative data alone; the decoder that reads it is T-058 and is not written.
//! Not supported: Layer I and Layer II, whose tables are not here either.
//! Role: This file owns the normative tables of ISO/IEC 11172-3 and 13818-3, and the derived decoding trees a test proves equivalent to them.
//
// @LICENCE: CC0-1.0 and Unlicence
// @ORIGIN: minimp3, https://github.com/lieff/minimp3 and PDMP3, https://github.com/technosaurus/PDMP3
// @MODIFIED: The normative tables of ISO/IEC 11172-3 were recovered from the packed decoding
// structures of both projects, checked against each other code by code, and rewritten in the form
// the standard prints them in. No code of either project is reproduced.
// @NOTICE: /bin/THIRDPARTY.md#mp3-normative-tables
#global namespace Mp3
#global internal

// Everything here is fixed by the format: a changed value changes what the decoder decodes.
//
// The Huffman tables are stated twice. `Huff<n>Len` and `Huff<n>Cod` are the normative form of
// Table B.7: the length and the value of the code word of every `(x, y)` pair, in `x`-major
// order, which is what a reader compares against the standard. `Huff<n>Tree` is the same
// information as a binary tree, which is what the decoder walks; `huffman.tables.test.swg` walks
// every code of the normative form through the tree and requires them to agree, so the derived
// form cannot drift from the stated one.

